WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.241
When Elon Musk sat in court and defended 
Tesla’s purchase of solar panel company SolarCity,

00:00:05.241 --> 00:00:09.770
he unleashed this bombshell: 
He hates being CEO of Tesla.

00:00:09.770 --> 00:00:15.000
He declared: "I rather hate it and I would much 
prefer to spend my time on design and engineering

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.000
which is what intrinsically I like doing.”

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:22.428
The man with the engineering mind has said 
he only spends 60% of his time at Tesla on engineering.

00:00:22.428 --> 00:00:24.887
So, why is he still in the driver’s seat?

00:00:24.887 --> 00:00:29.974
He said during the trial he strongly believes the electric 
car company cannot survive without him.

00:00:29.974 --> 00:00:33.807
Insisting: "...but I have to or frankly Tesla is going to die.” 

00:00:33.807 --> 00:00:38.692
But it’s come at a significant cost to himself. 
Here's what he's said about his experience.

00:00:38.692 --> 00:00:42.714
 I've had some pretty tough life experiences and Tesla's responsible for

00:00:42.714 --> 00:00:46.931
probably two-thirds of all personal 
and professional pain combined.”

00:00:46.931 --> 00:00:52.753
Musk always knew making Tesla a success would 
be a battle - giving it a 10% shot at pulling through.

00:00:52.753 --> 00:00:58.102
But he was inspired to try after test driving a tiny 
yellow electric prototype called the “tzero”.

00:00:58.102 --> 00:01:03.481
He encouraged the company behind the tzero, AC Propulsion, to commercialize it, and when it didn’t,

00:01:03.481 --> 00:01:06.607
that inspired Tesla to come up with the Tesla Roadster.

00:01:06.607 --> 00:01:12.485
The problem with leading an electric car company was that Musk already had a monumental task on his plate. 

00:01:12.485 --> 00:01:15.503
He had only just started his rocket 
company SpaceX which wanted to do 

00:01:15.503 --> 00:01:19.438
what nobody had done before: build reusable rockets.

00:01:19.438 --> 00:01:21.527
That was supposed to be his day job.

00:01:21.527 --> 00:01:26.399
And on the side, he thought he could dedicate some 
time to Tesla, maybe 20 to 30 hours a week

00:01:26.399 --> 00:01:28.020
to work on product engineering. 

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:32.774
Instead of 20 or 30 hours a week, he 
sometimes puts in 20 hours a day –

00:01:32.774 --> 00:01:37.815
even sleeping at Tesla’s factory when it struggled to 
mass-produce the Model 3 in 2018. 

00:01:37.815 --> 00:01:39.707
But he didn’t start out as CEO.  

00:01:39.707 --> 00:01:44.724
That job initially fell to engineer Martin Eberhard. 
He co-founded what was then Tesla Motors,

00:01:44.724 --> 00:01:47.389
in 2002 alongside Marc Tarpenning. 

00:01:47.389 --> 00:01:51.109
When they went looking for money to fund their 
venture, Musk came into the picture. 

00:01:51.109 --> 00:01:54.722
He invested his personal fortune and became 
Chairman of the Company’s board. 

00:01:54.722 --> 00:01:59.317
When production problems arose with the Roadster 
and Tesla nearly ran out of money,  

00:01:59.317 --> 00:02:01.282
Eberhard got ousted as CEO.

00:02:01.282 --> 00:02:03.846
Eventually, Musk took over, in 2008.

00:02:03.846 --> 00:02:08.104
He said it was too hard to find a qualified 
chief executive officer from outside 

00:02:08.104 --> 00:02:12.822
because Tesla wasn’t a traditional 
automaker but more of a technology start-up. 

00:02:12.822 --> 00:02:15.343
By that point, Tesla was near death. 

00:02:15.343 --> 00:02:20.568
Musk scrambled to save the company by cutting the 
workforce and relying on friends to cover payroll 

00:02:20.568 --> 00:02:23.531
while negotiating with investors to keep Tesla alive. 

00:02:23.531 --> 00:02:30.230
As he once told Kara Swisher on the podcast Recode 
Decode, he still can’t believe Tesla is alive.

00:02:30.230 --> 00:02:37.528
Elon Musk: It is absurd that Tesla is alive. Absurd. Absurd.
Kara Swisher: So what do you accredit that to? 

00:02:37.528 --> 00:02:40.373
Elon Musk: Excruciating effort. 
Kara Swisher: By you? 

00:02:40.373 --> 00:02:43.177
Elon Musk: 100-hour weeks. By everyone. 
Kara Swisher: By everyone here at Tesla.

00:02:43.177 --> 00:02:47.455
Elon Musk: Yes. There wasn’t some other way to do this. 

00:02:47.455 --> 00:02:53.345
He said during that especially hellish period in 2018 - he was open to someone else taking over at Tesla, 

00:02:53.345 --> 00:02:58.907
telling the New York Times: “If you have anyone who can do a better job, please let me know. They can have the job.”

00:02:58.907 --> 00:03:04.451
He reportedly did try to offer the top job to Volkswagen CEO Herbert Diess according to a report 

00:03:04.451 --> 00:03:06.364
by Business Insider Germany.

00:03:06.364 --> 00:03:10.560
This was before Diess left BMW to join Volkswagen in 2015.

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:13.094
There’s no word on why that didn’t work out. 

00:03:13.094 --> 00:03:19.087
Musk has pursued unorthodox strategies for growth 
as CEO. It’s laid out in Tesla’s “Master Plan”.

00:03:19.087 --> 00:03:24.747
The strategy involves releasing high-end models before more affordable ones whereas traditional automakers

00:03:24.747 --> 00:03:26.133
typically do the opposite. 

00:03:26.133 --> 00:03:30.000
After developing the Roadster, Tesla 
unveiled the Model S and Model X, 

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:33.950
which then paved the way for the more 
affordable Model 3 and Model Y. 

00:03:33.950 --> 00:03:39.620
Fun fact: Musk wanted to name the Model 3 
the Model E do that it really spells out SEXY but 

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:42.654
Ford had a trademark on the Model E 
and shut that down. 

00:03:42.654 --> 00:03:45.676
Musk has sometimes taken a cheeky approach to his role.

00:03:45.676 --> 00:03:49.703
He changed his job title to “Technoking of Tesla” 
whatever that means. 

00:03:49.703 --> 00:03:52.615
It could be a play on the word technology or techno.

00:03:52.615 --> 00:03:56.458
And he gave his Chief Financial Officer the title "Master of Coin".

00:03:56.458 --> 00:03:58.458
This is all part of the game plan. 

00:03:58.458 --> 00:04:03.698
He admitted his sense of humor generates free publicity 
for the company because the media loves this kind of thing. 

00:04:03.698 --> 00:04:06.220
But his antics have also gotten him into trouble.

00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:09.645
It didn’t go over well with the Securities and 
Exchange Commission when he tweeted

00:04:09.645 --> 00:04:12.909
he was thinking about taking Tesla private at $420 a share. 

00:04:12.909 --> 00:04:16.875
The stock has now soared well past $420 
even after splitting. 

00:04:16.875 --> 00:04:22.515
Tesla delivered 241,000 cars in the third quarter of 
2021, which means at this rate,

00:04:22.515 --> 00:04:25.329
it’s on track to hit a million deliveries a year.

00:04:25.329 --> 00:04:29.663
But success has come at the expense of 
a schedule Musk wanted to avoid. 

00:04:29.663 --> 00:04:32.104
And now, he’s hoping to dial back his duties a bit.

00:04:32.104 --> 00:04:35.823
He says he’ll likely skip Tesla’s 
quarterly earnings calls from now on. 

00:04:35.823 --> 00:04:43.294
“I will no longer be default doing earnings calls. 
I think going forward I will most likely not be on

00:04:43.294 --> 00:04:48.216
earnings calls unless there's something 
really important that I need to say."

00:04:48.216 --> 00:04:52.673
It’s in those conference calls that he’s made 
some epic and controversial comments, 

00:04:52.673 --> 00:04:56.229
like this exchange with a Wall Street analyst in 2018.
 

00:04:56.229 --> 00:04:59.534
Sanford C. Bernstein &amp; Co. analyst Antonio Sacconaghi: 
And, so, where specifically will you be in terms of...

00:04:59.534 --> 00:05:00.433
Elon Musk: Excuse me 

00:05:00.433 --> 00:05:01.501
Sacconaghi: ...capital requirement? 

00:05:01.501 --> 00:05:06.593
Musk: Next, next. Boring, 
 bonehead questions are not cool. Next. 

00:05:06.593 --> 00:05:13.320
He ended up apologizing to the analyst for his behavior. 
Despite taking this step back, we’ll still hear from him publicly. 

00:05:13.320 --> 00:05:18.324
He’s agreed to continuing doing interviews with 
YouTubers, however, he has pointed out this will be limited 

00:05:18.324 --> 00:05:20.575
as there’s only so much time in his day. 

00:05:20.575 --> 00:05:24.000
And time is precious if you’re trying to electrify the world. 

